  "reason": "The RNA encoder has proven to be the most impactful design choice: switching from pca_n2000 to scvi_n200 yielded +0.071 accuracy in the multimodal/vit_l setting (0.635→0.706). However, scgpt is completely untested across all experiments, leaving significant uncertainty about whether it could outperform scvi_n200. Config_049 (multimodal, multiprofile, scgpt, vit_l, avgpool, weighted) changes only the RNA encoder from the current best config (037), making it a clean single-variable test. If scgpt matches or exceeds scvi, it opens a new promising direction; if it falls short, it confirms scvi as the superior encoder and lets us focus remaining budget on aggregation or fusion refinements. This is the highest-information experiment available because it resolves the largest remaining uncertainty (encoder choice) in the context of the best-performing configuration."
}

